From 89bdd9a47e671b2733a787757bea3c047c351255 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gaosen <0x5e@sina.cn>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 01:28:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(bringup): stop claiming mutual authentication
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`supportsMutualAuthentication` describes the receiver, not the coprocessor: a
phone told yes answers /auth-setup with an `x-apple-at` header and an MFi4
body, and hangs up on a receiver that only knows the classic exchange. Claiming
nothing costs a receiver that does MFi4 — livi-cp — one extra round, which its
classic path answers all the same.

The field, the helper that decided it, and the parameter threaded through
`send_start` are gone.
